          </p>

          <p>
            The complaints we found center on digestion and texture. One reviewer said it still caused bloating, particularly alongside other rice-based foods, which is worth noting because XO Jacqui markets the product as reducing bloat. Rice protein in general has a reputation for a slightly gritty or chalky texture in water, and buyers of rice-based powders often report it mixes better in a blender than in a shaker. With no gums in the formula, XO Jacqui is likely to settle if left to stand.
          </p>

          <p>
            The Amazon listing did not show a usable rating or review count when we checked, so there is no large independent pool of buyer feedback to draw on yet. That is common for small direct-to-consumer brands, but it means taste and mixing are harder to judge than they are for Orgain or Garden of Life, which each have thousands of Amazon reviews.
