        <div id="who-should-buy" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            11. Who Should Buy XO Jacqui, and Who Should Skip It?
          </h2>

          <p>
            XO Jacqui suits a woman in midlife who wants a small, simple, dairy-free and soy-free shake with no stevia, sucralose or gums, already eats enough protein at meals, and has cleared the botanicals with her doctor. For that buyer, the six-ingredient label and monk fruit sweetening are genuine reasons to pay more.
          </p>

          <p>
            It is a poor fit for anyone whose main goal is protecting muscle and bone, because the 15 g dose and modest leucine make it a top-up rather than a meal's worth. It is also a poor fit for anyone on a budget, anyone who wants independent testing, and anyone taking hormone therapy, birth control or dopamine-related medication who has not checked chasteberry with a doctor. If symptom relief is the main reason you are looking, be clear that no ingredient here has strong evidence for hot flashes or sleep.
          </p>

          <p>
            Some women buy it because a menopause-specific product feels made for them, and that matters. But a protein powder does not need to be labeled for menopause to do the protein job. What helps most in midlife is getting enough protein at each meal, lifting weights two or three times a week, and getting enough calcium and vitamin D. Any of the alternatives above supports that as well as or better than XO Jacqui.
          </p>

          <p>
            If you decide to try it, choose Vanilla Greens if you want to avoid chasteberry, blend it with milk to raise the protein, and ask the brand for its heavy-metal test results. If you would rather start from a broader shortlist, our <a href="/best-protein-powder-for-menopause/">menopause protein powder rankings</a> and <a href="/best-plant-based-protein-powder/">best plant-based protein powder</a> guide cover options with more protein and published testing.
          </p>
